# The repository carries scripts only. Everything else is downloaded,
# built, generated, or specific to one host.

# Everything the build writes, all of it inside the clone:
#   downloads/  what it fetches, and the payloads packed from it
#   build/      the tables and their indexes
#   zim/        links to the archives, for kiwix
#   dist/       the two trees tools/make-dist.sh assembles
build/
downloads/
zim/
dist/

# The build's working directory: job lists, run logs, derived lists.
notes/

# A rampart installed inside the tree by tools/rampart-find.sh.
rampart/

# Written by setup.sh and tools/write-conf.sh: the address, the port and
# the citation base URL belong to the machine, not to the project.
# config.local.sh is the same idea for the build: where the big
# directories go on this particular disk.
config.local.sh
alpacalips.conf
web/server_conf.js
web/logs/
web/server.pid

# Leftovers.
*.bak*
*.pid
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# web/lib/corpus-inventory.js is generated by the merge stage and IS
# committed: it is what the MCP server tells a client the corpus holds,
# and a fresh clone should say the right thing before anyone builds.
